// Title: Visual Studio Code Tunnel Shell Execution
// ID: f4a623c2-4ef5-4c33-b811-0642f702c9f1
// Status: test
// Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-10-25
// Tags: attack.command-and-control, attack.t1071.001
// Description: Detects the execution of a shell (powershell, bash, wsl...) via Visual Studio Code tunnel. Attackers can abuse this functionality to establish a C2 channel and execute arbitrary commands on the system.
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

((src.process.parent.image.path containsCIS "\\servers\\Stable-" AND src.process.parent.image.path endswithCIS "\\server\\node.exe" AND src.process.parent.cmdline containsCIS ".vscode-server") AND (((src.process.image.path endswithCIS "\\powershell.exe" OR src.process.image.path endswithCIS "\\pwsh.exe") AND src.process.cmdline containsCIS "\\terminal\\browser\\media\\shellIntegration.ps1") OR ((src.process.image.path endswithCIS "\\wsl.exe" OR src.process.image.path endswithCIS "\\bash.exe"))))
